311 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 213 0 R
/E (Menstrual health is increasingly recognised as a critical public health, education, and gender equality issue. Yet across Africa, millions of women and girls continue to face barriers that prevent them from managing menstruation safely, confidently, and with dignity. These barriers extend beyond the affordability of menstrual products to include inadequate water, sanitation and hygiene \(WASH\) facilities, limited menstrual health education, restricted access to healthcare, persistent social stigma, and policy gaps.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [34]
>>
endobj
312 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 213 0 R
/E (The State of Menstrual Equity in Africa 2026 provides an evidence-based overview of the current menstrual health landscape across the continent. Drawing on research from international organisations, peer-reviewed literature, and African case studies, the report examines how systemic inequalities shape menstrual experiences and why addressing them is essential for achieving sustainable development.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [35]
>>
endobj
