559 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 227 0 R
/E (Although menstruation is a natural biological process, societies have historically treated it as a private matter rather than an issue connected to public health, education, equality, and human rights. This silence has influenced how women and girls experience their periods, shaping access to information, healthcare, sanitation, and social support.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
560 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 227 0 R
/E (For many years, menstruation was rarely discussed in policy spaces, schools, or healthcare systems. The absence of conversation contributed to a lack of research, limited investment, and insufficient attention to the challenges faced by millions of menstruating people worldwide.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
